The [[Fortree Gym]] specializes in {{type|Flying}} Pokémon. Flying-type moves are super effective against {{t|Bug}}-, {{t|Fighting}}-, and {{type|Grass}} Pokémon, while Flying-type Pokémon are weak to {{t|Electric}}-, {{t|Ice}}-, and {{type|Rock}} moves.

The Gym features a series of turnstiles. These barriers must be rotated and approached from alternate directions in order to progress. Pass through the first turnstile and battle Bird Keeper Jared. Push the second turnstile counter-clockwise to battle Picnicker Kylee, then clockwise to its starting position. In the east-central area, push the L-shaped turnstile counter-clockwise. Rotate the T-shaped one counter-clockwise. Loop around and move the L-shaped turnstile two places clockwise. Loop back around and move the T-shaped one clockwise. Go west to battle Camper Terrell, then continue north. In the northeast area, move the southern turnstile clockwise. Turn the eastern one counter-clockwise, then back to its starting position. Battle Bird Keeper Will. Move the western one clockwise, the southern one counter-clockwise, and the eastern one counter-clockwise. Pass by Bird Keeper Will a second time and go west to reach the [[Gym Leader]].

[[Winona]] leads with her {{p|Swellow}}, a speedy {{2t|Normal|Flying}} Pokémon. Avoid inflicting status ailments, as its {{a|Guts}} Ability boosts its physical {{stat|Attack}} by 50% under such conditions. Her {{p|Pelipper}} is more defensive, and can hinder the its target with [[status move]]s. As a {{2t|Water|Flying}} Pokémon, it is most vulnerable to {{t|Electric}} attacks. Like most {{type|Steel}} Pokémon, {{p|Skarmory}} has high physical {{stat|Defense}}, and its {{m|Steel Wing}} attack can boost it further. It takes serious damage from {{t|Fire}}- and Electric-type attacks, which fortunately target its weaker {{stat|Special Defense}} instead. Finally, her {{p|Altaria}} is naturally a more defensive Pokémon, but {{m|Dragon Dance}} increases both its Attack and {{stat|Speed}} by one stage each. It sustains massive damage from {{t|Ice}} attacks, but {{t|Rock}}- and {{type|Dragon}} moves are effective, as well. Avoid using a Rock-type Pokémon against it, as Altaria can fight back with {{m|Earthquake}}!

